---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const updated = 'July 31, 2026';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | The Engine Room Financial Group"
  description="How The Engine Room Financial Group collects, uses, and protects personal and mobile information, including text message appointment reminder programs operated on behalf of client healthcare facilities."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  intro="How we collect, use, and protect personal information — including mobile phone numbers enrolled in the text message appointment reminder programs we operate for the healthcare facilities we serve."
  updated={updated}
>
  <section>
    <div class="legal-callout">
      <p>
        This policy governs ERFG&rsquo;s <strong
          >text message appointment reminder programs</strong
        > and the personal information handled by them. Separately, the bank accounts
        that ERFG connects through Plaid for internal cash reporting are covered by
        our <a href="/privacy/bank-balance-dashboard"
          >Bank Balance Dashboard privacy policy</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">01</span>Who We Are</h2>
    <p>
      The Engine Room Financial Group (&ldquo;ERFG,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo;
      &ldquo;us,&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;) is an outsourced financial and
      administrative operations company located at 456A Central Ave Suite 115,
      Cedarhurst, NY 11516.
    </p>
    <p>
      Among the services we provide, ERFG operates <strong
        >text message appointment reminder programs on behalf of the healthcare
        facilities we contract with</strong
      >. When you receive an appointment reminder text message from one of those
      programs, the message is sent by ERFG on behalf of the facility named in
      the message. That facility remains responsible for your care; ERFG
      administers the messaging program on its behalf under a written services
      agreement.
    </p>
    <p>
      This policy governs those programs. An individual facility may publish its
      own program notice describing facility-specific details; where any such
      notice conflicts with this policy, this policy governs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">02</span>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      For the appointment reminder programs, we collect and process only what is
      needed to send and support reminder messages:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name</li>
      <li>Your mobile phone number</li>
      <li>
        The date, time, and location of your scheduled appointment, and the name
        of the facility
      </li>
      <li>
        The content of your replies to our messages, including confirmation
        replies (such as YES or NO) and program commands (such as STOP or HELP)
      </li>
      <li>
        Message delivery records, such as whether a message was delivered and
        when
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not collect payment card information, Social Security numbers, or
      clinical records through these messaging programs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">03</span>Where This Information Comes From</h2>
    <p>
      Your mobile phone number is provided by you, in writing, on a signed
      consent form presented to you at the facility. Appointment details come
      from the facility&rsquo;s own scheduling system, and only for patients who
      have signed that consent form.
    </p>
    <p>
      Enrollment is voluntary. Consent to receive text messages is never a
      condition of receiving care, scheduling an appointment, being admitted, or
      completing any purchase or transaction.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">04</span>How We Use It</h2>
    <p>We use this information solely to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Send you reminders about your scheduled appointments</li>
      <li>Notify you when an appointment is rescheduled or cancelled</li>
      <li>Process your confirmation replies and pass them to the facility</li>
      <li>Respond to HELP requests and honor STOP requests</li>
      <li>Maintain records of consent and opt-out as required by law</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong
        >We do not use your information for marketing, promotional, or
        advertising purposes</strong
      >, and we do not send marketing or promotional messages through these
      programs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">05</span>Mobile Information Sharing</h2>
    <div class="legal-callout">
      <p>
        No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates
        for marketing or promotional purposes. Information sharing to
        subcontractors in support services, such as customer service, is
        permitted. All other use case categories exclude text messaging
        originator opt-in data and consent; this information will not be shared
        with any third parties.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information or your mobile phone number. We
      do not rent, trade, or otherwise disclose your mobile information to data
      brokers, advertisers, or affiliates for their own use.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">06</span>Service Providers</h2>
    <p>
      We use Twilio Inc. as our messaging provider to transmit text messages to
      your wireless carrier. Twilio processes your mobile phone number and
      message content only to deliver messages on our behalf, is bound by
      contract to maintain confidentiality, and is not permitted to use your
      information for its own purposes.
    </p>
    <p>
      We share information with the facility that scheduled your appointment,
      because that facility is the originator of the communication and your
      provider of care. We do not share your information with any other third
      party except where required by law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">07</span>HIPAA and Protected Health Information</h2>
    <p>
      Appointment information relating to your treatment is protected health
      information under the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act
      (HIPAA). In operating these programs, <strong
        >ERFG acts as a business associate of each facility</strong
      > under HIPAA, pursuant to an executed Business Associate Agreement, and our
      messaging infrastructure is configured for HIPAA-eligible use.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use and disclose protected health information only as permitted by that
      agreement and by HIPAA — here, to send treatment-related appointment
      reminders. Your rights with respect to your protected health information,
      including the right to access and amend it, are described in the Notice of
      Privacy Practices provided to you by your facility.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please note that standard SMS text messaging is not an encrypted channel.
      Reminder messages are kept deliberately minimal for this reason, and
      contain no diagnosis or clinical detail. You may decline enrollment or opt
      out at any time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">08</span>How Long We Keep It</h2>
    <p>
      We retain your mobile phone number for as long as you remain enrolled in
      the program. When you opt out or ask to be removed, your mobile number is
      removed from the active reminder system within one business day.
    </p>
    <p>
      We retain a minimal record of your consent and of your opt-out — the fact
      of it and its date — for as long as required to demonstrate compliance
      with telecommunications and healthcare recordkeeping obligations.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">09</span>Your Choices</h2>
    <h3>Stop receiving messages</h3>
    <p>
      Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to any message from the program. You will
      receive one confirmation message and then no further messages. Opting out
      will not affect your care, your appointments, or your standing with your
      facility in any way.
    </p>
    <h3>Get help</h3>
    <p>
      Reply <strong>HELP</strong> to any message, or contact your facility
      directly. For Perkins Country Manor outpatient therapy, call
      <a href="tel:6067562156">(606) 756-2156</a>.
    </p>
    <h3>Access, correct, or delete your information</h3>
    <p>
      Contact your facility, or contact us at
      <a href="mailto:getintouch@TheERFG.com">getintouch@TheERFG.com</a>. If
      your request concerns protected health information, we will coordinate
      with your facility, which is the covered entity responsible for
      responding.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">10</span>Security</h2>
    <p>
      We maintain administrative, technical, and physical safeguards designed to
      protect the information described in this policy against unauthorized
      access, use, or disclosure. Access is limited to personnel who need it to
      operate the program.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">11</span>Children</h2>
    <p>
      These programs are not directed to children under 13, and we do not
      knowingly enroll a child under 13. Where a patient is a minor, enrollment
      is completed by the parent or legal guardian, whose mobile number receives
      the reminders.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">12</span>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we change this policy, we will update the effective date shown above
      and post the revised policy at this address. Material changes affecting
      the messaging programs will be communicated through the facilities we
      serve.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">13</span>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy, or about a text message you received, can be
      directed to us at
      <a href="mailto:getintouch@TheERFG.com">getintouch@TheERFG.com</a> or
      <a href="tel:5168780015">(516) 878-0015</a>. The terms governing the
      messaging program itself are available at
      <a href="/terms">theerfg.com/terms</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
